//! Fixed regression positions for the CLI's `bench search` command.
//!
//! Position 1 is the start position; positions 2–4 are midgame positions
//! from seeded random walks (24, 40 and 63 plies in) so captures, promotions
//! and igui moves are exercised. Positions 2 and 3 are black-to-move,
//! position 4 is white-to-move.
//!
//! **Never edit these strings in place.** The whole point of `bench search`
//! is that its node counts and `bench hash` line only change when the
//! engine's behaviour changes; replacing a position invalidates every
//! historical comparison. If a position turns out to be terminal or
//! illegal on some future rules change, replace it with a freshly generated
//! one (e.g. `nnue explain <net> --plies N --seed S` prints its position)
//! and record that in the commit message.

